# Profile: offline
# DNS-denies EVERYTHING for the bricked clients except the allowlist below.
#
# !! THIS IS NOT A FIREWALL !!
# DNS denial only stops name lookups. On the bricked devices the following
# still work and this is expected, not a bug:
#   - already-open connections, until they are closed
#   - anything cached in the OS/browser DNS cache until the TTL expires
#   - apps that connect to hard-coded IP addresses
#   - VPNs, Tor, and apps using DNS-over-HTTPS/TLS to their own resolver
#   - iCloud Private Relay / Android Private DNS
#   - offline/downloaded content, and cellular data on the phone
#
# The catch-all below uses the wildcard form. The @allow entries are emitted
# as @@ exception rules, which take priority over the block in AdGuard.

@blockall

# --- Emergency / infrastructure allowlist ---
# Keep this SHORT and justified. Everything here stays reachable while offline.

@allow fritz.box
                        # Router admin UI. Without this you cannot reach the
                        # router by name to undo anything. fritz.box is the
                        # AVM FRITZ!Box name; replace it with your own router's
                        # local name (routerlogin.net, tplinkwifi.net, ...).
@allow raspberrypi.local
                        # Add your Pi's own <hostname>.local here too if you
                        # changed the hostname.
@allow briq.home
                        # The Pi itself, so the controller status page and the
                        # QR/NFC confirmation links keep working. Without this
                        # you could not switch back OUT of offline from a phone.
                        # The QR/NFC codes use the raw IP and need no DNS at
                        # all - briq.home is convenience only, so a DNS
                        # problem can never lock you out of the escape hatch.
@allow local
                        # mDNS/.local name resolution on the LAN.
@allow fritz.nas
@allow fritz.repeater
                        # Other local names your router serves, harmless and
                        # occasionally needed to reach network hardware.
                        # Delete these two if you have no FRITZ! hardware.

# --- Time sync ---
@allow pool.ntp.org
@allow ntp.org
@allow time.cloudflare.com
@allow time.apple.com
@allow time.windows.com
                        # Without working NTP, devices can drift and then fail
                        # TLS certificate validation, which turns a temporary
                        # focus block into a confusing broken-internet state.

# --- Deliberately NOT allowlisted ---
# Push notification services (APNs, FCM) are blocked in this profile. That is
# the point: no notifications. Emergency phone calls and SMS go over the
# cellular network and are completely unaffected by any of this.
